{"availability":"available","full":"elixir-lotus/lotus","name":"lotus","description":"Embeddable business intelligence engine for Elixir — SQL editor, dashboards, charts, and AI query generation that mount directly in   your Phoenix app.","category":"Business","language":"Elixir","stars":84,"forks":10,"created":"2025-08-09T16:40:00Z","updated":"2026-10-05T09:35:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hexdocs.pm/lotus/readme.html","topics":[],"demo":"https://demo.lotusbi.com/lotus","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.691Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.691Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.691Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.691Z","stars":84,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The embeddable BI engine for Elixir apps — query editor, dashboards, visualizations, and AI-powered query generation that mount directly in your Phoenix app. SQL and non-SQL data sources behind one pluggable adapter contract. No Metabase. No Redash. No extra infrastructure.","Every app eventually needs analytics, reporting, or an internal SQL tool. The usual options — Metabase, Redash, Grafana — mean another service to deploy, another auth system to sync, another thing to keep running.","Lotus takes a different approach: it mounts inside your Phoenix app. Add the dependency, run a migration, add one line to your router, and you have a full BI interface — query editor, charts, dashboards — running on your existing infrastructure. Read-only by design, production-safe from day one."],"features":["Query editor with syntax highlighting, autocomplete, and real-time execution","Query management — save, organize, and reuse queries with descriptive names","Smart variables — parameterize queries with {{variable}} syntax, configurable input widgets, and query-backed dropdown options. Each adapter owns its own substitution, so prepared-statement engines bind parameters while…","Visualizations — 5 chart types (bar, line, area, scatter, pie) with renderer-agnostic config DSL","Dashboards — combine queries into interactive views with 12-column grid layouts, filters mapped onto query variables, auto-refresh, and public sharing via secure tokens"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elixir-lotus/lotus/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f529579086ef4b97f6075dad73b80b348b88bfd1851d0152c1b801f118f11b46","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.809Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.809Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The embeddable BI engine for Elixir apps — query editor, dashboards, visualizations, and AI-powered query generation that mount directly in your Phoenix app. SQL and non-SQL data sources behind one pluggable adapter contract. No Metabase. No Redash. No extra infrastructure.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elixir-lotus/lotus/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f529579086ef4b97f6075dad73b80b348b88bfd1851d0152c1b801f118f11b46","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elixir-lotus/lotus/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.810Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T09:35:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elixir-lotus/lotus/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:17.811Z","hash":"f529579086ef4b97f6075dad73b80b348b88bfd1851d0152c1b801f118f11b46","originalBytes":16238,"storedBytes":16238,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["query","lotus","source","elixir","data","statement","main","adapter","yes","adapters","schema","see","guide","queries","result","config","guides","read-only","repo","select","sources","sql","visibility","app","results","table","any","auth","column","count","elasticsearch","get","mix","myapp.repo","own","run","separate","syntax","tables","web","add","analytics","built","cache","clickhouse","configurable","controls","custom","dashboards","editor","engines","error","execution","free","full","generation","json","